  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Finely chop the brown onion. Finely grate the garlic. Rinse the red lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-a7062cd2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large saucepan, heat the butter and a drizzle of olive oil over a medium-high heat. Cook the onion, stirring, until softened, 3-4 minutes.\n• Add the ginger paste and garlic and cook until fragrant, 1 minute. Add a drizzle more olive oil and add the Bengal curry paste, tomato paste and turmeric. Cook, stirring, until fragrant, 2 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-89653bad.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add the water, the salt, red lentils and coconut milk to the pan. Stir to combine. Cover with a lid, reduce the heat to medium and cook until the lentils have softened, 20-25 minutes. Grate the carrot. Roughly chop the tomato. In the last 10 minutes of cook time, remove the lid and stir through the carrot and tomato. Continue cooking until the lentils and veggies have softened.\n• TIP: Add a splash of water if the dhal looks dry.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-9b38e8b0.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the dhal is cooking, heat olive oil (2 tbs for 2 people / 1/4 cup for 4 people) in a medium frying pan over a medium-high heat. Add a pinch of chilli flakes (if using) to the oil and cook until fragrant, 1 minute. Transfer the chilli-infused oil to a small bowl. Brush (or spread using the back of a spoon) some chilli oil over both sides of a mini flour tortilla. Return the pan to a medium\u0002high heat and add the tortilla. Cook until golden, 1 minute each side. Transfer to a plate lined with paper towel and repeat with the remaining tortillas (see ingredients).",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-8f632211.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Once the lentils and veggies have softened, stir through the baby spinach leaves until just wilted.\n• Season with salt and pepper. Pick and roughly chop the mint leaves.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-59c5c535.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the creamy coconut dhal between bowls, top with Greek-style yoghurt and sprinkle with mint. Serve with the chilli flatbreads.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60c858dde2cf84527272a974/step-978d61a2.jpg"
    }
  ]
